136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (409A valuations are 99% of the time performed by a third-party, which is considered to be the safest way. If you do not have safe harbor and the IRS audit determines your common stock is mispriced, your employees would be taxed an extra 20% fine on the difference in value plus any additional penalties. In order to avoid this, most companies choose to play safe and appoint a third party valuer to conduct their 409A valuation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
